ull\n      labels:\n        app: user-service\n        service: user-service\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - command:\n        - UserService\n        image: docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest\n        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n        name: user-service\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 9090\n          protocol: TCP\n        resources: {}\n        terminationMessagePath: /dev/termination-log\n        terminationMessagePolicy: File\n        volumeMounts:\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/jaeger-config.yml\n          name: user-service-config\n          subPath: jaeger-config.yml\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/service-config.json\n          name: user-service-config\n          subPath: service-config.json\n      dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst\n      hostname: user-service\n      restartPolicy: Always\n      schedulerName: default-scheduler\n      securityContext: {}\n      terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30\n      volumes:\n      - configMap:\n          defaultMode: 420\n          name: user-service\n        name: user-service-config\nstatus:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T18:41:48Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T18:41:48Z"\n    message: Deployment has minimum availability.\n    reason: MinimumReplicasAvailable\n    status: "True"\n    type: Available\n  - lastTransitionTime: "2026-03-17T18:41:30Z"\n    lastUpdateTime: "2026-03-17T18:41:48Z"\n    message: ReplicaSet "user-service-559b79c875" has successfully progressed.\n    reason: NewReplicaSetAvailable\n    status: "True"\n    type: Progressing\n  observedGeneration: 2\n', id='b702c8b2-76d8-474c-a2e5-c398a1aa9046', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-9804e6b835f2c931'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='224426a0-26d5-43ba-a6c2-57c3f5958d7c'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user-service deployment has replicas set to 0, which is why it\'s not running. The previous steps showed that the deployment was scaled up to 1 but then scaled down to 0. The next step is to find out why the replicas are at 0. \n\nLooking at the deployment YAML, the replicas are explicitly set to 0. But why? Maybe there\'s a config error, or perhaps a rollout issue. I should check the events in the deployment to see if there\'s any error messages. The events from earlier showed a scaling up and then scaling down. \n\nWait, the user might have manually adjusted the replicas, or there could be a problem with the pod template. Let me check the pod template\'s image. The image is docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest. Maybe the image isn\'t pulling correctly. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the ConfigMap referenced in the volumeMounts is missing or misconfigured. The ConfigMap is named user-service. If that\'s missing, the pod might fail to start, leading the deployment to scale down. \n\nI should check the ConfigMap to see if it exists and has the necessary files. Also, checking the logs of the pod would help. But since the pod isn\'t running, maybe the image pull is failing. Let me try pulling the image manually or checking the image pull policy. The imagePullPolicy is IfNotPresent, so if the image isn\'t present locally, it won\'t pull. \n\nWait, but the deployment was scaled up once, so maybe the initial pull failed. Let me check the events for any image pull errors. The previous events didn\'t show that. Alternatively, maybe the pod is failing to start due to a configuration issue in the ConfigMap. \n\nAnother angle: the deployment\'s status shows that the replica set was created but then scaled down. Maybe there\'s a resource limit issue, but the resources are empty in the container specs. \n\nI need to check the logs of the pod if it exists. But since the pod isn\'t running, maybe the logs aren\'t available. Alternatively, check the events in the deployment for more details. The events showed scaling up and down, but no specific errors. \n\nWait, maybe the ConfigMap is missing. Let me check if the ConfigMap \'user-service\' exists in the namespace. If it\'s missing, the pod can\'t start, leading to the deployment scaling down. So I should check the ConfigMap\'s existence and its contents. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the image is incorrect. Let me verify the image name and tag. The image is docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest. Maybe the tag is wrong or the image isn\'t available. \n\nI should also check the pod\'s status in the events. Since the pod isn\'t running, maybe there\'s an error in the pod\'s creation. Let me try to get the pod\'s details if it exists. But the previous \'get pods\' didn\'t show any user-service pods. \n\nSo, the next step is to check the ConfigMap \'user-service\' in the social-network namespace. If it\'s missing, that\'s a problem. Also, check the image pull policy and see if the image is accessible. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the deployment was rolled back or there\'s a typo in the deployment name. But the deployment name is correct. \n\nSo, the root cause is likely the ConfigMap missing or the image not being available. Let me check the ConfigMap first.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get configmap user-service -n social-network"  \nThe user-service deployment references a ConfigMap named "user-service" in its volume mounts. If this ConfigMap is missing or misconfigured, the pod may fail to start, leading to the deployment scaling down to 0 replicas. Checking its existence and contents will confirm if this is the root cause.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 803, 'prompt_tokens': 5131, 'total_tokens': 5934, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_re